<!-- Problem Section -->
<section class="problem-section">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="section-tag">The Problem</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align:center;">You Are Paying for 5-10 Tools That Don't Talk to Each Other</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">A website builder here, a CRM there, a booking tool, an email platform, a payment processor, an analytics dashboard. None of them connected. All of them billing you separately.</p>
    <div class="highlight-box fade-in">
      <ul>
        <li>The average small business spends $500-$2,000/month on disconnected SaaS tools</li>
        <li>You manually copy customer data between systems because nothing integrates</li>
        <li>Payments happen in one tool, customer records live in another, and your website is a third</li>
        <li>Each tool has its own login, its own billing cycle, and its own support team</li>
        <li>You are paying for features you do not use across multiple platforms</li>
        <li>Over a year, that is $6,000-$24,000 spent on software fragmentation</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Solution Section -->
<section class="solution-section">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="section-tag">The Solution</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align:center;">One Platform. Everything Connected.</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Payments, website, CRM, booking, email marketing, and analytics — all integrated. No more juggling tools. No more manual data entry.</p>
    <div class="solution-copy fade-in">
      <p>When a customer books an appointment on your website, their information flows into your CRM, a confirmation email goes out automatically, and when they pay, the transaction is linked to their customer record, your invoicing, and your reporting dashboard. No manual reconciliation. No exporting CSV files to figure out who paid what.</p>
      <p>We use Stripe Connect under the hood — the same payment infrastructure trusted by millions of businesses — so you get enterprise-grade security and reliability. But unlike using Stripe by itself, every payment is connected to your entire business system.</p>
      <p>The real savings come from eliminating 5-10 separate subscriptions. When your website, CRM, booking, email marketing, payments, and analytics all live in one place, you stop paying $500-$2,000/month in fragmented SaaS fees.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

